WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.941 --> 00:00:19.210
Dr. Dolittle, Polynesia, Tommy, and Charles all peered into the dark cave entrance.

2
00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:22.592
"Hello?" called out the doctor.

3
00:00:22.612 --> 00:00:26.034
"Hello?" came back the echo.

4
00:00:26.054 --> 00:00:30.036
"Maybe we should go inside," the doctor said.

5
00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:34.885
But before they took a step, a tall dark shadow appeared.

6
00:00:35.605 --> 00:00:37.906
It was the great Indian Long Arrow.

7
00:00:38.486 --> 00:00:41.267
He was the tallest man Tommy had ever seen.

8
00:00:41.987 --> 00:00:45.328
He wore a brightly woven cloth round his lower body.

9
00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:48.429
He carried a large pouch around his waist.

10
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:52.251
Something heavy inside was pulling the pouch downward.

11
00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:56.652
In his hair was a beautiful eagle's feather.

12
00:00:57.672 --> 00:01:01.794
The Indian's eyes were sharp and full of wisdom, just like an eagle's.

13
00:01:02.774 --> 00:01:05.375
He blinked them a few times and stared at Dr.

14
00:01:05.395 --> 00:01:07.316
Dolittle. Dr.

15
00:01:07.356 --> 00:01:08.677
Dolittle was speechless.

16
00:01:08.697 --> 00:01:13.518
"Well, I, so he stuttered.

17
00:01:14.319 --> 00:01:16.660
The tall Indian did not say a word.

18
00:01:18.641 --> 00:01:19.581
Finally, Dr.

19
00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:23.723
Dolittle took a deep breath and said, "It's a great pleasure to meet you, Long Arrow."

20
00:01:24.743 --> 00:01:26.764
Long Arrow did not open his mouth.

21
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.523
"Oh, how silly of me," gushed the doctor.

22
00:01:30.543 --> 00:01:32.945
"You don't understand me.

23
00:01:33.965 --> 00:01:36.648
Let's see the doctor thought for a moment.

24
00:01:37.789 --> 00:01:42.192
Then he started to speak in dog language: "I am Dr.

25
00:01:42.272 --> 00:01:46.416
Dolittle." The Indian did not understand dog talk.

26
00:01:46.436 --> 00:01:50.479
"I can also speak other animal languages," Dr.

27
00:01:50.519 --> 00:01:52.160
Dolittle said in horse talk.

28
00:01:53.221 --> 00:01:56.084
The Indian blinked twice but remained silent.

29
00:01:58.028 --> 00:02:00.250
"Dr. Dolittle," interrupted Tommy.

30
00:02:01.231 --> 00:02:02.452
The doctor shook his head.

31
00:02:02.472 --> 00:02:04.253
"Not now, Tommy."

32
00:02:04.974 --> 00:02:11.279
Then he tried pig talk: "I have heard many great things about you," he said to the Indian.

33
00:02:12.199 --> 00:02:13.841
The Indian scratched his ear.

34
00:02:13.861 --> 00:02:15.742
"Um, Doctor?"

35
00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.283
Tommy whispered again.

36
00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:20.866
"What is it, Tommy?"

37
00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.248
The doctor turned to him impatiently.

38
00:02:23.268 --> 00:02:26.291
"Maybe he understands the eagles' language?"

39
00:02:26.631 --> 00:02:27.752
Tommy said shyly.

40
00:02:28.668 --> 00:02:29.729
The doctor nodded.

41
00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.972
In eagle talk he said, "Can you understand me now?"

42
00:02:35.013 --> 00:02:38.256
The Indian's eyes suddenly became warm and friendly.

43
00:02:38.276 --> 00:02:45.322
"At last, we can understand each other," Long Arrow said in the eagle language.

44
00:02:46.422 --> 00:02:52.007
Dr. Dolittle and Long Arrow exchanged a long, deep conversation using eagle talk.

45
00:02:53.348 --> 00:02:54.729
Charles covered his ears.

46
00:02:54.749 --> 00:02:58.012
"It sounds like screaming," he said to Tommy.

47
00:02:58.720 --> 00:02:59.620
Tommy agreed.

48
00:03:00.761 --> 00:03:05.743
But Polynesia told them that eagle talk was one of the most beautiful bird languages.

49
00:03:05.763 --> 00:03:10.045
"We have brought you some food and water," the doctor said.

50
00:03:10.065 --> 00:03:15.247
"Thank you," replied Long Arrow as he took the things from the doctor.

51
00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:19.789
But rather than eat and drink, he walked back into the cave.

52
00:03:20.829 --> 00:03:23.570
Dr. Dolittle and Tommy followed him inside.

53
00:03:24.331 --> 00:03:27.532
Polynesia and Charles stayed back at the cave entrance.

54
00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:32.422
It took a while for Tommy's eyes to get used to the dark.

55
00:03:33.143 --> 00:03:36.285
Long Arrow led them to two men lying on the ground.

56
00:03:37.146 --> 00:03:40.048
A little bit of light came through a crack in the ceiling.

57
00:03:41.149 --> 00:03:43.870
Tommy could see that the men were very sick.

58
00:03:45.772 --> 00:03:48.594
Long Arrow said something to them in his native tongue.

59
00:03:49.294 --> 00:03:51.796
Then he opened his pouch and took something out.

60
00:03:52.657 --> 00:03:54.738
It looked like plants and a heavy stone.

61
00:03:55.559 --> 00:03:57.140
He poured water on the plants.

62
00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.561
Then he scraped them against the stone to make a paste.

63
00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:03.402
He put the paste on the men's foreheads.

64
00:04:04.962 --> 00:04:08.543
The two men slowly sat up and said something to Long Arrow.

65
00:04:09.344 --> 00:04:10.924
Tommy watched in amazement.

66
00:04:11.924 --> 00:04:13.645
The Indian spoke, and Dr.

67
00:04:13.685 --> 00:04:14.865
Dolittle translated.

68
00:04:14.885 --> 00:04:18.066
"He says the men's pain is gone now."

69
00:04:18.086 --> 00:04:23.728
"It's time to go home," continued Long Arrow, still speaking in eagle talk.

70
00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.681
Long Arrow and Dr.

71
00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:29.763
Dolittle helped the two men walk toward the cave entrance.

72
00:04:30.604 --> 00:04:31.945
Tommy carried their things.

73
00:04:31.965 --> 00:04:36.087
"Come to our village," said one man in a weak voice.

74
00:04:36.107 --> 00:04:40.230
"We are grateful to you for saving us," said the other.

75
00:04:41.071 --> 00:04:44.593
But when they reached the entrance, trouble was waiting for them.

76
00:04:47.195 --> 00:04:51.058
A group of the unfriendly natives had tied up Charles and Polynesia.

77
00:04:51.818 --> 00:04:54.240
They pointed their swords at the cave's entrance.

78
00:04:55.008 --> 00:04:56.069
When they saw Dr.

79
00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:58.531
Dolittle, they walked toward him angrily.

80
00:04:58.551 --> 00:05:00.873
"Oh no," whispered the doctor.

81
00:05:00.893 --> 00:05:02.714
"What are we going to do?"
